{% comment %}
  sections/product-bundle.liquid

  Build-your-own-bundle: a category-filtered product list on one side, a tray of
  slots on the other, and a discount that grows as the tray fills.

  ## Why it is not `sections/bundle-builder.liquid`

  Bundle builder is a paginated product *grid* with a list of slots beside it —
  a collection page with a tray bolted on. This is the arrangement in the
  drawings: a short, curated, category-switched list of wide rows, and a tray
  that is the centrepiece rather than a sidebar. The two have different markup at
  every level, so they are two sections and a merchant picks the one that matches
  what they are selling. Neither is deleted by the other.

  What they do share is the honest part, and they share it by construction — see
  "The discount is display only" below.

  ## The two drawings, and which one this is

  
  `Bundle Product-1` gives every slot a discount label: 10%, 15%, 25%, 30%, 35%,
  40%, escalating as the tray fills. `Bundle Product-2` drops the labels, puts a
  free-shipping bar in their place, and gives each filled slot a quantity
  stepper.

  Both are here, behind **Tray style**, because they are not the same offer:

    ladder    Design 1. The reason to add a sixth product is a bigger discount.
              One `Amount off products` automatic discount per tier in Shopify
              admin, each with its own minimum quantity, and no app.

    quantity  Design 2. The reason to add a sixth product is that you want six.
              One automatic discount, or none at all.

  Ladder is the default because it is the stronger offer and because the theme
  already has the settings for it.

  ## The discount is display only, and the section says so

  A theme cannot create a discount. There is no storefront API that prices a cart
  differently, and the Theme Store rejects a theme that tries — a cart that
  disagrees with checkout is worse than no discount at all.

  So what happens here is: the tray shows the tier the customer has reached, the
  lines are added to the cart with `_bundle_discount` on them, and the money comes
  off at checkout through an automatic discount the merchant creates in
  **Discounts**. The **Discount tiers** panel says exactly that, on the panel,
  where a merchant setting the percentages will read it.

  Per-slot labels are read as *unlocks*, not as per-item pricing, for the same
  reason: a Shopify discount applies to the order, so a slot badge saying "25%
  Off" has to mean "filling this slot unlocks 25% off" or it is a claim about a
  line that will not be true at checkout. Reached tiers are marked; unreached
  ones are dimmed and marked as locked.

  ## The shell is `sections/expert-quote.liquid`'s, setting id for setting id

  Container, colour scheme, background media, the four border widths, the two
  sets of corners, the gaps behind a Desktop/Mobile switch, the margins, the
  stack layer and the whole spacing group. Every id here is one that section
  already carries, and both reach them through `snippets/spacing.liquid`,
  `snippets/background-media.liquid` and `snippets/container.liquid`.

  ## Everything inside it is a block

    Header      `blocks/section-header.liquid` through `content_for 'block'` —
                editable, undeletable, undraggable. A section called Product
                bundle whose heading has been dragged into the tray is a section
                a merchant can break by accident.

    The rest    `{% content_for 'blocks' %}`, and the tree is the merchant's:

                  Group ── Tabs ── Category
                                   Category
                                   Category
                  Group ── Build your own bundle
                           Slot box
                           Bundle total

  This used to be a picker column and a tray welded into this file, with the
  categories as the only blocks — so "the tabs" and "the tray" were positions in
  a template, and there was exactly one arrangement of this section in the
  world. A merchant who wanted the tray above the picker, or a Text block
  between the heading and the boxes, had nowhere to put it.

  Now `<product-bundle>` is a flex row of whatever the merchant put in it. Every
  `data-ref` the component reads — the slots, the note, the total, the submit —
  is collected from anywhere inside the element, so which block renders which
  piece is not something `assets/product-bundle.js` has to know.

  ## Most of the settings did not move with the markup

  Card height, rows on screen, the tier ladder, the tray's wording: all still
  `section.settings`, read by the blocks. Moving them into the blocks would have
  emptied every one of them on every store already running this section, in
  exchange for a tree that renders exactly the same. The blocks are the
  arrangement; the section is still the design.

  Two groups *did* go, both for the same reason — two settings doing one job are
  two settings that can disagree:

    to the Group    The tray's width, background, corners, padding and Sticky on
                    desktop. A **Group** already offers all five, and offers
                    them better.

    to Bundle tabs  The whole **Category tabs** panel — the four pill colours,
                    the border, the corners, the height, the type, the space
                    between the pills and between the strip and the products.
                    They belong to the strip, not to the section around it, and
                    a section with two strips in it can now have two designs.
                    `blocks/product-bundle-tabs.liquid` writes the same
                    `--bundle-tab-*` properties this file used to.
{% endcomment %}

{%- liquid
  assign s = section.settings

  comment
    ---- the background ----

    The colour scheme's, until the merchant says otherwise: either a colour, or a
    picture behind the whole section. Emitted as a real `background` shorthand
    rather than a custom property because `color-scheme-container` paints a
    background *and* a gradient image, and only the shorthand clears both.
  endcomment
  assign background_media = s.background_media | default: 'none'
  assign has_background_media = false
  if background_media != 'none'
    assign has_background_media = true
  endif

  assign background_paint = ''
  if has_background_media == false
    assign background_paint = s.background_color | default: ''
  endif

  comment
    ---- the frame ----

    One width per side, summed into `border_any` so the three properties are
    emitted only when at least one side is drawn. Opacity goes into the colour
    rather than onto the element: `opacity` on the section would fade the tray
    along with its frame.

    Identical to `sections/expert-quote.liquid` and `sections/featured-offer.liquid`
    by construction, not by coincidence.
  endcomment
  assign border_line = s.border_style | default: 'none'

  assign bw_top = 0
  assign bw_right = 0
  assign bw_bottom = 0
  assign bw_left = 0
  assign border_any = 0

  if border_line != 'none'
    assign bw_top = s.border_width_top | default: 0 | plus: 0
    assign bw_right = s.border_width_right | default: 0 | plus: 0
    assign bw_bottom = s.border_width_bottom | default: 0 | plus: 0
    assign bw_left = s.border_width_left | default: 0 | plus: 0
    assign border_any = bw_top | plus: bw_right | plus: bw_bottom | plus: bw_left

    assign border_percent = s.border_opacity | default: 100 | plus: 0
    if s.border_color == blank
      assign border_paint = 'color-mix(in srgb, currentColor ' | append: border_percent | append: '%, transparent)'
    else
      assign border_alpha = border_percent | divided_by: 100.0
      assign border_paint = s.border_color | color_modify: 'alpha', border_alpha
    endif
  endif

  comment
    ---- corners ----

    Four corners, twice, behind the same Desktop/Mobile switch the padding and
    the gaps already use. A phone gets its own four because 40px is a soft lift
    across 1400px and a heavy scoop out of a 390px screen. Each mobile corner
    falls back to its desktop value when the setting is missing entirely, so a
    section saved before these existed keeps one shape at every width.
  endcomment
  assign r_tl = s.border_radius_top_left | default: 0 | plus: 0
  assign r_tr = s.border_radius_top_right | default: 0 | plus: 0
  assign r_bl = s.border_radius_bottom_left | default: 0 | plus: 0
  assign r_br = s.border_radius_bottom_right | default: 0 | plus: 0

  assign r_tl_m = s.border_radius_top_left_mobile | default: r_tl | plus: 0
  assign r_tr_m = s.border_radius_top_right_mobile | default: r_tr | plus: 0
  assign r_bl_m = s.border_radius_bottom_left_mobile | default: r_bl | plus: 0
  assign r_br_m = s.border_radius_bottom_right_mobile | default: r_br | plus: 0

  assign margin_top = s.margin_top | default: 0 | plus: 0
  assign margin_bottom = s.margin_bottom | default: 0 | plus: 0

  comment
    ---- the gaps ----

    A Desktop/Mobile pair behind one switch, the shape every other section in the
    theme uses. Both pairs are published unconditionally and `assets/base.css`
    picks which applies at a given width, because the pair the merchant is not
    looking at in the editor is still the pair the other breakpoint renders.

    `plus: 0` rather than `default` alone, which would replace a deliberate 0.
  endcomment
  assign gap_x = s.gap_horizontal | default: 48 | plus: 0
  assign gap_y = s.gap_vertical | default: 16 | plus: 0
  assign gap_x_mobile = s.gap_horizontal_mobile | default: gap_x | plus: 0
  assign gap_y_mobile = s.gap_vertical_mobile | default: gap_y | plus: 0

  comment
    ---- the tray ----

    `slots` is how many boxes are drawn. `tray_style` decides whether each box
    carries a tier badge (the first drawing) or a quantity stepper (the second).
  endcomment
  assign slots = s.bundle_size | default: 6 | plus: 0
  assign tray_style = s.tray_style | default: 'ladder'

  comment
    ---- the tiers ----

    Six checkbox-and-percentage pairs, one per slot, rather than a free-text
    field: a merchant typing "3:30, 4:40" gets it wrong once and then cannot see
    why the bar never moves.

    They are serialised into one `quantity:percent` attribute for the component,
    which stays agnostic about how many tiers exist — the same contract
    `assets/bundle-builder.js` already reads, so the two sections describe a tier
    ladder the same way.

    Only tiers that fall within the tray are published. A tier at 6 items on a
    four-slot tray is a promise the tray cannot keep.
  endcomment
  assign tier_parts = ''
  for i in (1..6)
    assign enable_key = 'tier_' | append: i | append: '_enable'
    assign percent_key = 'tier_' | append: i | append: '_percent'

    if s[enable_key] and i <= slots
      assign tier_parts = tier_parts | append: i | append: ':' | append: s[percent_key] | append: ','
    endif
  endfor
  assign tiers = tier_parts | split: ',' | join: ','

  comment
    The element is a flex row and nothing more. Which side the tray is on used
    to be a select here that swapped a grid's columns; it is the order of two
    Groups now, which is both more direct and more capable — a merchant who
    wants the tray above the picker at every width can say that too, and could
    not before.
  endcomment
  assign layout_classes = 'product-bundle__layout'
-%}

{%- capture section_style -%}
  {%- render 'spacing', section: s, declarations: true -%}
  --product-bundle-radius: {{ r_tl }}px {{ r_tr }}px {{ r_br }}px {{ r_bl }}px;
  --product-bundle-radius-mobile: {{ r_tl_m }}px {{ r_tr_m }}px {{ r_br_m }}px {{ r_bl_m }}px;
  --product-bundle-margin-block-start: {{ margin_top }}px;
  --product-bundle-margin-block-end: {{ margin_bottom }}px;
  --product-bundle-gap-x: {{ gap_x }}px;
  --product-bundle-gap-y: {{ gap_y }}px;
  --product-bundle-gap-x-mobile: {{ gap_x_mobile }}px;
  --product-bundle-gap-y-mobile: {{ gap_y_mobile }}px;
  --product-bundle-slot-columns: {{ s.slot_columns | default: 3 }};
  --product-bundle-accent: {{ s.accent_color | default: '#03D26F' }};
  {%- comment -%}
    The tab strip's design is not here any more.

    Its four colours, its border, its corners, its height and its type are all
    settings on `blocks/product-bundle-tabs.liquid`, which writes the same
    `--bundle-tab-*` properties onto its own element. A strip styles itself,
    and a section with two of them can have two different ones — which it could
    not when the numbers lived up here.

    The cascade still runs three deep and no rule has to know which level won:

      the pill's own   `style=` from the Category block
      the strip's      the same property on the Tabs block
      the scheme's     the fallback written into each `var()` in base.css
  {%- endcomment -%}
  {%- comment -%}
    The card's height and the space between two of them, as lengths, because
    that is what CSS needs and what `carousel-vars` is handed for
    `--carousel-gap`. The carousel's own height is built from them in
    `assets/base.css` against the slide count the architecture already writes.

    The image inside the card is not set here. It is the card's height less the
    padding above and below it, which is how `Bundle-Porduct-Card.svg` is drawn
    — 145 less twice 17.5 is 110 — so the two can never be set to numbers that
    do not fit each other.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  --product-bundle-row-size: {{ s.row_height | default: 145 }}px;
  --product-bundle-row-gap: {{ s.row_gap | default: 13 }}px;
  --product-bundle-row-size-mobile: {{ s.row_height_mobile | default: 124 }}px;
  --product-bundle-row-gap-mobile: {{ s.row_gap_mobile | default: 12 }}px;
  --product-bundle-card-padding-block: {{ s.card_padding | default: 17.5 }}px;
  --product-bundle-card-radius: {{ s.card_radius | default: 24 }}px;
  --product-bundle-media-radius: {{ s.media_radius | default: 14 }}px;
  {%- comment -%}
    ---- the product card's colours ----

    Four, in two pairs: what a card is made of, and what it becomes once it is
    in the bundle.

    Each is emitted only when the merchant has set it, for the reason the tab
    strip's four colours are — a property that exists but is empty invalidates
    the whole declaration it is used in, so the card would lose its background
    rather than fall through to the next level. Absence is what lets the level
    below apply, and there are three of those: the card's own colour here, the
    colour scheme the card carries (**Card colour scheme**, which is what the
    `color-scheme-container` on each `<li>` resolves), and the section's scheme
    behind that.

    The foreground is one setting and not four, and it reaches the title, both
    prices, the dotted rule and the add control through `--bundle-card-ink` in
    `assets/base.css`. Those all read `--color-heading` when nothing is set
    here, which is exactly what they read before this setting existed — so an
    untouched card is unchanged, and a merchant who sets one colour does not
    then have to find the other three.

    The selected pair is separate because a card in the bundle is a state rather
    than a variant: it was an accent ring on the same surface, which is legible
    on a pale card and invisible on a dark one. The ring colour is now the
    merchant's too, and still falls back to the section's accent.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  {%- if s.card_background != blank -%}
    --product-bundle-card-background: {{ s.card_background }};
  {%- endif -%}
  {%- if s.card_foreground != blank -%}
    --product-bundle-card-foreground: {{ s.card_foreground }};
  {%- endif -%}
  {%- if s.card_active_background != blank -%}
    --product-bundle-card-active-background: {{ s.card_active_background }};
  {%- endif -%}
  {%- if s.card_active_foreground != blank -%}
    --product-bundle-card-active-foreground: {{ s.card_active_foreground }};
  {%- endif -%}
  {%- if s.card_active_border != blank -%}
    --product-bundle-card-active-border: {{ s.card_active_border }};
  {%- endif -%}
  {%- if border_any > 0 -%}
    --product-bundle-border-width: {{ bw_top }}px {{ bw_right }}px {{ bw_bottom }}px {{ bw_left }}px;
    --product-bundle-border-style: {{ border_line }};
    --product-bundle-border-color: {{ border_paint }};
  {%- endif -%}
  {%- if background_paint != '' -%}
    background: {{ background_paint }};
  {%- endif -%}
{%- endcapture -%}

<div
  class="product-bundle color-scheme-container color-{{ s.color_scheme | default: 'scheme-1' }}{% if has_background_media %} has-background-media{% endif %}"
  data-section-spacing
  {%- if s.stack_layer != blank and s.stack_layer != 'default' %} data-section-layer="{{ s.stack_layer }}"{% endif %}
  data-section-id="{{ section.id }}"
  style="{{ section_style | strip_newlines | strip }}"
>
  {%- if has_background_media -%}
    {% render 'background-media', settings: s %}
  {%- endif -%}

  <div class="product-bundle__inner {% render 'container', width: s.container_width %}">
    {% content_for 'block', type: 'section-header', id: 'product-bundle-header' %}

    <product-bundle
      class="{{ layout_classes }}"
      data-section-id="{{ section.id }}"
      data-size="{{ slots }}"
      data-tiers="{{ tiers }}"
      data-tray-style="{{ tray_style }}"
      data-max-per-product="{{ s.max_per_product | default: 4 }}"
      data-require-full="{{ s.require_full }}"
      data-bundle-id="bundle-{{ section.id }}"
      data-bundle-label="{{ s.tray_heading | escape }}"
      data-quick-add="{{ settings.enable_quick_add }}"
    >
      {%- comment -%}
        ---------- what the merchant arranged ----------

        One `content_for 'blocks'`, and that is the whole of the layout.

        This used to be a picker column and a tray welded together here, with the
        categories as the section's only blocks — so "the tabs" and "the tray"
        were positions in a template rather than things a merchant could move,
        and there was exactly one arrangement of this section in the world.

        Now the pieces are blocks and the arrangement is theirs:

          Group ───── Tabs ───── Category
                                 Category
                                 Category
          Group ───── Build your own bundle
                      Slot box
                      Bundle total

        Two Groups side by side is the drawing. One Group, or three, or the tray
        above the picker on a phone, are all the same blocks in a different
        order — and a Text block, an Image or a set of Buttons drop in anywhere
        among them, because a Group takes any block in the theme.

        `<product-bundle>` stays the element around all of it. Every `data-ref`
        the component reads — the slots, the note, the total, the submit — is
        collected from anywhere inside it, so which block renders which piece is
        not something `assets/product-bundle.js` has to know.
      {%- endcomment -%}
      {% content_for 'blocks' %}
    </product-bundle>
  </div>
</div>

{% schema %}
{
  "name": "t:sections.product_bundle.name",
  "tag": "section",
  "class": "section",
  "blocks": [
    {
      "type": "@theme"
    },
    {
      "type": "@app"
    }
  ],
  "settings": [
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "t:sections.product_bundle.paragraphs.blocks"
    },
    {
      "type": "select",
      "id": "container_width",
      "label": "t:shared.container.width.label",
      "info": "t:shared.container.width.info",
      "options": [
        { "value": "edge", "label": "t:shared.container.width.options__1.label" },
        { "value": "wide", "label": "t:shared.container.width.options__2.label" },
        { "value": "standard", "label": "t:shared.container.width.options__3.label" },
        { "value": "compact", "label": "t:shared.container.width.options__4.label" },
        { "value": "custom", "label": "t:shared.container.width.options__5.label" }
      ],
      "default": "standard"
    },

    { "type": "header", "content": "t:sections.product_bundle.headers.tray" },
    { "type": "paragraph", "content": "t:sections.product_bundle.paragraphs.tray" },
    {
      "type": "select",
      "id": "tray_style",
      "label": "t:sections.product_bundle.settings.tray_style.label",
      "info": "t:sections.product_bundle.settings.tray_style.info",
      "options": [
        { "value": "ladder", "label": "t:sections.product_bundle.settings.tray_style.options__1.label" },
        { "value": "quantity", "label": "t:sections.product_bundle.settings.tray_style.options__2.label" }
      ],
      "default": "ladder"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "tray_heading",
      "label": "t:shared.heading.label",
      "default": "Build Your Own Bundle"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "tray_subheading",
      "label": "t:sections.bundle_builder.settings.subheading.label",
      "default": "Mix Match. Save more"
    },
    {
      "type": "select",
      "id": "tray_icon",
      "label": "t:sections.product_bundle.settings.tray_icon.label",
      "options": [
        { "value": "none", "label": "t:shared.options.none" },
        { "value": "bag", "label": "Bag" },
        { "value": "cart", "label": "Cart" },
        { "value": "tag", "label": "Tag" },
        { "value": "heart", "label": "Heart" },
        { "value": "shield", "label": "Shield" },
        { "value": "star", "label": "Star" }
      ],
      "default": "bag"
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "bundle_size",
      "label": "t:sections.bundle_builder.settings.bundle_size.label",
      "min": 2,
      "max": 8,
      "step": 1,
      "default": 6
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "slot_columns",
      "label": "t:sections.product_bundle.settings.slot_columns.label",
      "min": 2,
      "max": 4,
      "step": 1,
      "default": 3
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "max_per_product",
      "label": "t:sections.product_bundle.settings.max_per_product.label",
      "info": "t:sections.product_bundle.settings.max_per_product.info",
      "min": 1,
      "max": 8,
      "step": 1,
      "default": 4,
      "visible_if": "{{ section.settings.tray_style == 'quantity' }}"
    },
    {
      "type": "checkbox",
      "id": "require_full",
      "label": "t:sections.product_bundle.settings.require_full.label",
      "info": "t:sections.product_bundle.settings.require_full.info",
      "default": false
    },
    {
      "type": "checkbox",
      "id": "show_progress",
      "label": "t:sections.product_bundle.settings.show_progress.label",
      "default": true
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "t:sections.product_bundle.paragraphs.tray_group"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "tray_note",
      "label": "t:sections.product_bundle.settings.tray_note.label",
      "info": "t:sections.product_bundle.settings.tray_note.info",
      "default": "Add more product to unlock bigger discounts"
    },
    {
      "type": "select",
      "id": "tray_note_icon",
      "label": "t:sections.product_bundle.settings.tray_note_icon.label",
      "options": [
        { "value": "none", "label": "t:shared.options.none" },
        { "value": "tag", "label": "Tag" },
        { "value": "truck", "label": "Truck" },
        { "value": "info", "label": "Info" },
        { "value": "clock", "label": "Clock" }
      ],
      "default": "tag"
    },
    {
      "type": "richtext",
      "id": "disclaimer",
      "label": "t:sections.bundle_builder.settings.disclaimer.label",
      "info": "t:sections.bundle_builder.settings.disclaimer.info"
    },

    { "type": "header", "content": "t:sections.bundle_builder.headers.discounts" },
    { "type": "paragraph", "content": "t:sections.product_bundle.paragraphs.discounts" },
    {
      "type": "checkbox",
      "id": "tier_1_enable",
      "label": "t:sections.product_bundle.settings.tier_enable.label_1",
      "default": true,
      "visible_if": "{{ section.settings.tray_style == 'ladder' }}"
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "tier_1_percent",
      "label": "t:sections.product_bundle.settings.tier_percent.label_1",
      "min": 0, "max": 70, "step": 5, "unit": "%", "default": 10,
      "visible_if": "{{ section.settings.tray_style == 'ladder' and section.settings.tier_1_enable }}"
    },
    {
      "type": "checkbox",
      "id": "tier_2_enable",
      "label": "t:sections.product_bundle.settings.tier_enable.label_2",
      "default": true,
      "visible_if": "{{ section.settings.tray_style == 'ladder' }}"
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "tier_2_percent",
      "label": "t:sections.product_bundle.settings.tier_percent.label_2",
      "min": 0, "max": 70, "step": 5, "unit": "%", "default": 15,
      "visible_if": "{{ section.settings.tray_style == 'ladder' and section.settings.tier_2_enable }}"
    },
    {
      "type": "checkbox",
      "id": "tier_3_enable",
      "label": "t:sections.product_bundle.settings.tier_enable.label_3",
      "default": true,
      "visible_if": "{{ section.settings.tray_style == 'ladder' }}"
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "tier_3_percent",
      "label": "t:sections.product_bundle.settings.tier_percent.label_3",
      "min": 0, "max": 70, "step": 5, "unit": "%", "default": 25,
      "visible_if": "{{ section.settings.tray_style == 'ladder' and section.settings.tier_3_enable }}"
    },
    {
      "type": "checkbox",
      "id": "tier_4_enable",
      "label": "t:sections.product_bundle.settings.tier_enable.label_4",
      "default": true,
      "visible_if": "{{ section.settings.tray_style == 'ladder' }}"
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
